For folks wondering how the current DoS fares compared to where we were at the end of July then there is not much difference flag-wise at least:

![relayflags-Running-Exit-Fast-Guard-Stable-HSDir-2026-05-23-2026-10-21](/uploads/ff5d780d44128c96c0357b2d08d2b107/relayflags-Running-Exit-Fast-Guard-Stable-HSDir-2026-05-23-2026-10-21.png){width=576 height=360}

The amount of relays with `Stable` and `Guard` flags is a bit lower now but then the network is smaller now as well compared to end of July/begin of August. Additionally, the number of relays with the `HSDir` flag was lower back then.

As someone coming here might wonder how this DoS compares to the big previous ones (like the one at the end of 2022 and around May 2024), there are crucial differences. Firstly, back then those DoS attacks were heavily affecting our users, but not so this time. For that claim, check out the performance data graphed below:

![torperf-onion-2022-06-18-2026-09-16-5mb](/uploads/ccb889f55270d937b5cb51b87010c44b/torperf-onion-2022-06-18-2026-09-16-5mb.png){width=576 height=360}

